==============================================================================
S1  (i) root asymmetry: summand companions of the odd arrows, both sheets
==============================================================================
halved reading   (T-form, k=1 arrow): n -> n + c,  c_+ = (n+1)/2,  c_- = (n-1)/2
unhalved reading (C/E-form arrow):    n -> n + c,  c_+ = 2n+1,     c_- = 2n-1
strict summand arrow needs: companion c positive and c != n

n | halved c_+ status | halved c_- status | unhalved c_+ status | unhalved c_- status
1 | companion 1 = n: DIAGONAL (excluded) | companion 0 not positive: NOT AN ARROW | strict | companion 1 = n: DIAGONAL (excluded)
3 | strict | strict | strict | strict
5 | strict | strict | strict | strict
7 | strict | strict | strict | strict
9 | strict | strict | strict | strict

odd n <= 1000000 where the arrow is not a strict summand arrow:
  halved plus    : [1]
  halved minus   : [1]
  unhalved plus  : []
  unhalved minus : [1]
PROVED (algebra): (n+1)/2 = n iff n = 1; (n-1)/2 <= 0 iff n = 1; 2n+1 = n never (n>0); 2n-1 = n iff n = 1.
So the strict-summand shadow differs between the sheets ONLY at n = 1, and in a reading-dependent way:
  halved:   plus 1 -> 2 is the excluded diagonal (1,1); minus 1 -> 1 has companion 0 (not an arrow)
  unhalved: plus 1 -> 4 = 1 + 3 is strict;              minus 1 -> 2 = 1 + 1 is the excluded diagonal

companion family: the k=1 companion map n -> (n+b)/2 is the a=1 member of (a n + b)/2^k;
1 is a fixed point of (a n + b)/2^k iff a + b is a power of two:
  (a,b)=(3, 1): a+b= 4 -> 1 fixed: True
  (a,b)=(3,-1): a+b= 2 -> 1 fixed: True
  (a,b)=(1, 1): a+b= 2 -> 1 fixed: True
  (a,b)=(1,-1): a+b= 0 -> 1 fixed: False
  (a,b)=(5, 1): a+b= 6 -> 1 fixed: False
  (a,b)=(5,-1): a+b= 4 -> 1 fixed: True
  (a,b)=(7, 1): a+b= 8 -> 1 fixed: True
  (a,b)=(7,-1): a+b= 6 -> 1 fixed: False

cycle arrows, halved reading (k=1 steps are summand arrows n -> n + (n+b)/2; k>=2 steps are descents):
  sheet +1 cycle (1,): 1->1 (k=2, fixed point, companion 0)
  sheet -1 cycle (1,): 1->1 (k=1, companion 0, NOT AN ARROW)
  sheet -1 cycle (5, 7): 5->7 (k=1, companion 2, strict); 7->5 (k=2, descent)
  sheet -1 cycle (17, 25, 37, 55, 41, 61, 91): 17->25 (k=1, companion 8, strict); 25->37 (k=1, companion 12, strict); 37->55 (k=1, companion 18, strict); 55->41 (k=2, descent); 41->61 (k=1, companion 20, strict); 61->91 (k=1, companion 30, strict); 91->17 (k=4, descent)

