==============================================================================
S3  (iii) E_- (arrows n -> n/2 for even n, n -> 3n-1 for all n): Q1_- and Q2_- to 10^6
==============================================================================
T_- basin census, odd n <= 1000000: basin{1} 163486, basin{5,7} 162122, basin{17..91} 174392, escapes 0, max steps to drop 125
E_- path 5 -> 1 with 15 arrows verified; even->3n-1 arrows used: [(10, 29)]
  path: 5 -> 14 -> 7 -> 20 -> 10 -> 29 -> 86 -> 43 -> 128 -> 64 -> 32 -> 16 -> 8 -> 4 -> 2 -> 1
E_- path 17 -> 1 with 35 arrows verified; even->3n-1 arrows used: [(68, 203), (304, 911)]
  path: 17 -> 50 -> 25 -> 74 -> 37 -> 110 -> 55 -> 164 -> 82 -> 41 -> 122 -> 61 -> 182 -> 91 -> 272 -> 136 -> 68 -> 203 -> 608 -> 304 -> 911 -> 2732 -> 1366 -> 683 -> 2048 -> 1024 -> 512 -> 256 -> 128 -> 64 -> 32 -> 16 -> 8 -> 4 -> 2 -> 1
Q1_- (every n reaches 1 in E_-): FINITE-EXACT for n <= 1000000: each n halves to an odd n' <= n, n' reaches a cycle
  under T_- (census above, T_- steps are E_- paths), and the three cycle minima reach 1 by the paths above.
Q2_- greedy G_-(m) = (2^k m + 1)/3, k minimal with result an integer not 0 mod 3, starts 2 <= m <= 1000000, 3 !| m: 666666
  certified below m: 666665; hit 1 first: 1; cycled: [4]; capped: 0
  steps-to-certify histogram (first six): [(1, 444444), (2, 148147), (3, 24692), (4, 24691), (5, 5487), (6, 8230)] max steps 35
  m = 4: G_- cycles on {4, 11}; but 1 -> 2 -> 4 is not an E_- path (2 -> 4 is not an arrow); 4 is reached from 8,
  and 8 <- 16 <- 32 <- 11 <- 4 ... the E_- cycle 4->11->32->16->8->4; 1 reaches 4 via 1->2->5->14->7->20->10->29->86->43->128->64->32->16->8->4
  (verified, 15 arrows). Hence Q2_- holds for all m <= 1000000, 3 !| m: FINITE-EXACT.
VERDICT: Q1_- and Q2_- both hold to 10^6, so the one-giant-SCC picture of E is SHEET-BLIND: E_- has it too,
  while T_- has three cycles; the cycles are escaped through even->3n-1 arrows (the path lists above).

